Subject: [PATCH 10/23] refactor: rewire backtesting/backtest.py, remove
 import-time side effects
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Wraps the former top-level script in run_backtest(), guarded by
if __name__ == '__main__' — the module previously connected to MT5
and ran a full backtest as a side effect of being imported, which is
incompatible with it (or main.py, which now imports it transitively
via shared conventions) ever being unit tested.

Replaces print() with structured logging.

Fixes the same class of dead imports as main.py: 'get_market_data' and
'add_indicators' don't exist (real names: MarketData class,
calculate_indicators). Also documents that BacktestEngine.execute_trade
itself calls approve_trade() and simulate_trade() with the wrong
number of arguments for their current signatures — independent of
this file, and out of scope for this milestone (Milestone 2b).

run_backtest() now stops after loading data and computing indicators,
returning the DataFrame, rather than running a trade-simulation loop
that would immediately raise TypeError.

Adds tests/test_backtest_runner.py covering the error paths and the
import-time-side-effect regression.
